204
00:08:35,048 --> 00:08:36,482
Sara's mom: Uh-huh.

205
00:08:36,482 --> 00:08:37,784
Sara: TO THE POINT
WHERE I COULD--

206
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:38,717
Sara's mom: Is there a doctor
there to kind of watch--

207
00:08:38,717 --> 00:08:40,520
Sara: I DIDN'T EVEN
ASK FOR ONE.

208
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,389
I WAS JUST, LIKE,
"I DON'T WANT TO DEAL WITH IT."

209
00:08:42,389 --> 00:08:43,490
Sara's mom: How does
it feel today?

210
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:44,591
Sara: IT'S OKAY.

211
00:08:44,591 --> 00:08:45,658
IT'S JUST REALLY SORE.

212
00:08:45,658 --> 00:08:46,960
Sara's mom: Oh, honey...

213
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,795
Sara: MY KNEE
IS ALWAYS A DISCOMFORT.

214
00:08:48,795 --> 00:08:51,031
ON A SCALE OF ONE TO TEN,
IT'S ABOUT A FOUR.

215
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:52,098
I'VE JUST LEARNED
TO LIVE WITH IT.

216
00:08:52,098 --> 00:08:53,533
IT'S JUST REALLY HARD.

217
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:01,474
Shandi: I MISS MY BOYFRIEND.
I DO. I WISH--I REALLY WISH

218
00:09:01,474 --> 00:09:03,510
HE COULD HAVE EXPERIENCED THIS
WITH ME, EVEN THOUGH I KNOW

219
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,712
HE WOULDN'T EXPERIENCE IT
THE SAME WAY.

220
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:06,813
(phone dialing)

221
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:10,917
(phone ringing)

222
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:12,819
Shandi: HELLO.

223
00:09:12,819 --> 00:09:15,422
Eric: Do you remember
a girl named Lauren and...

224
00:09:15,422 --> 00:09:17,057
Shandi: OH, YOU HUNG OUT
WITH SOME GIRLS?

225
